# Beat for demo step "Hidden bits": the answer riding home (spec 0396).
#
# The companion to beats/smuggle. That beat decoded "whoami" out of a
# captured *response*; this one is the matching *request*, carrying Bob's
# answer "experiment" through the same padded-varint channel, from row 1,
# cell 1 (the grid is the request's field 1 too). The mechanism is already
# understood, so there are no wire-level steps: one step per letter for the
# first six letters, e x p e r i — 48 bits, all in row 1 as long as the
# grid is at least 48 cells wide (Bob's window at least 96 columns) — then
# the reassembled word, whose last four letters spill past that point and
# are read the same way. Advance with space or Enter.
#
# Step text is written for a 120-column line (spec 0400).
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh), on the matching request capture:
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc capture/NNNNNN-request.pb \
#       --script beats/smuggle2

title: The answer rides home

steps:
